<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">16 January in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 16 January, from 1362 to 2003.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/north-sea" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/north-sea.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1362 CE <span class="tih-ago">664 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The 'Great Drowning of Men' storm surge hits the North Sea coast</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A severe south-westerly gale drove the sea over the coasts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/low-countries">Low Countries</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a>. At least 25,000 people died, and the trading town of Rungholt vanished beneath the waves.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/low-countries">Low Countries</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-sea">North Sea</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1547 CE <span class="tih-ago">479 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ivan IV crowned the first Tsar of All Russia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Aged 16, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-iv-of-russia">Ivan IV</a> was crowned in the Kremlin's Dormition Cathedral with the title of tsar. His reign brought the conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kazan">Kazan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/astrakhan">Astrakhan</a> as well as the terror of the oprichnina.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1780 CE <span class="tih-ago">246 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Rodney defeats the Spanish in the 'Moonlight Battle'</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Admiral <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-brydges-rodney-1st-baron-rodney">George Rodney</a>'s larger British fleet overwhelmed a Spanish squadron off Cape St Vincent in an unusual night action. The victory allowed him to resupply besieged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gibraltar">Gibraltar</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gibraltar">Gibraltar</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1919 CE <span class="tih-ago">107 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ratification of the Eighteenth Amendment sets up Prohibition</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Nebraska became the 36th state to ratify the amendment banning the manufacture and sale of alcohol, making it part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constitution-of-the-united-states">US Constitution</a>. Prohibition took effect a year later and lasted until 1933.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1920 CE <span class="tih-ago">106 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">League of Nations Council holds its first meeting</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The League's Council met for the first time in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>, at the French Foreign Ministry. The League settled some minor disputes but failed to stop aggression in the 1930s.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-nations">League of Nations</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1945 CE <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hitler moves into the Führerbunker in Berlin</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adolf-hitler">Adolf Hitler</a> took up residence in the air-raid shelter beneath the Reich Chancellery garden. He directed the final months of the war from there and killed himself in the bunker on 30 April.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1969 CE <span class="tih-ago">57 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Soyuz 4 and Soyuz 5 make the first crewed docking</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Two Soviet spacecraft docked in orbit and two cosmonauts spacewalked from Soyuz 5 to Soyuz 4. It was the first exchange of crew between spacecraft, a rehearsal for building space stations.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">2003 CE <span class="tih-ago">23 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Space Shuttle Columbia launches on its final mission</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Columbia lifted off on mission STS-107 with seven astronauts. Foam debris struck its wing during launch, and the shuttle broke apart on re-entry sixteen days later, killing the crew.</p></div></li></ol>
